      "problem": "Given $f(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{6-x}}{\\sqrt{2x}},$ find $f(4).$",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $x$ with $4$ in the given expression, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6-4}}{\\sqrt{2(4)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{8}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{8}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1}}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
